<div class="tve-page-section-in tve_empty_dropzone" data-css="tve-u-1801743132f" style=""><div class="thrv_wrapper thrv-columns" data-css="tve-u-180188bf72c" style="--tcb-col-el-width: 924.667;"><div class="tcb-flex-row v-2 tcb--cols--2" data-css="tve-u-17fb6870260" style=""><div class="tcb-flex-col ui-resizable-resizing" data-css="tve-u-180173f99c9" style=""><div class="tcb-col" data-css="tve-u-18018891b04" style=""><div class="thrv_wrapper tve_image_caption" data-css="tve-u-17fb686c78c" style=""><span class="tve_image_frame" style=""><img alt="addiction services, Dr Crawford TMS" center-h-t="false" center-v-d="false" class="tve_image tcb-moved-image wp-image-2962" data-css="tve-u-17fb686c78d" data-height="393" data-id="2962" data-init-height="508" data-init-width="584" data-width="452" decoding="async" height="393" loading="lazy" ml-d="0" ml-m="0" ml-t="-79" mt-d="0" mt-m="0" sizes="auto, (max-width: 452px) 100vw, 452px" src="wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Dr.-Cyntrell.jpg" srcset="wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Dr.-Cyntrell.jpg 584w, wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Dr.-Cyntrell-300x261.jpg 300w" style="aspect-ratio: auto 584 / 508;" title="Dr. Cyntrell" width="452"/></span></div></div></div><div class="tcb-flex-col" style=""><div class="tcb-col" style=""><grammarly-extension class="dnXmp" data-grammarly-shadow-root="true" style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; pointer-events: none; --rem: 16;"></grammarly-extension><grammarly-extension class="dnXmp" data-grammarly-shadow-root="true" style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; pointer-events: none; --rem: 16;"></grammarly-extension><grammarly-extension class="dnXmp" data-grammarly-shadow-root="true" style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; pointer-events: none; --rem: 16;"></grammarly-extension><grammarly-extension class="dnXmp" data-grammarly-shadow-root="true" style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; pointer-events: none; --rem: 16;"></grammarly-extension><grammarly-extension class="dnXmp" data-grammarly-shadow-root="true" style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; pointer-events: none; --rem: 16;"></grammarly-extension><grammarly-extension class="dnXmp" data-grammarly-shadow-root="true" style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; pointer-events: none; --rem: 16;"></grammarly-extension><div class="thrv_wrapper thrv_text_element kbth1ybs" data-css="tve-u-17fb686dd01" style=""><h4 class="" data-css="tve-u-17fb686dd02" style=""><span data-css="tve-u-17fb686dd03"><span data-css="tve-u-18018895294">Cyntrell Crawford</span><span data-css="tve-u-18018895297">,</span> <span data-css="tve-u-18018895299">M.D.</span></span></h4></div><div class="thrv_wrapper thrv_text_element" data-css="tve-u-17fb686f32e" style=""><h2 class="" data-css="tve-u-19446b36715" dir="ltr" style="">Dr. Crawford - Psychiatrist in Reading</h2><p dir="ltr"><strong>Dr. Crawford</strong> is an adult psychiatrist specializing in psychiatry, TMS therapy, addiction, and recovery. She earned her <strong>Doctorate of Medicine</strong> from the <strong>Tulane University School of Medicine</strong> in New Orleans and completed her internship and residency at the <strong>University of Texas Health Sciences Center</strong> at the Houston Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences. </p><p dir="ltr">Dr. Crawford has practiced medicine for ten years and has treated <strong>over 25,000 patients</strong>. She is Reading's <strong>premier TMS provider</strong>, offering a customized program for all her patients. With a particular interest in patients facing challenging situations, Dr. Crawford has dedicated her life to the rigorous treatment of <a class="" data-css="tve-u-19446b45c28" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mental_disorder" style="outline: none;" target="_blank">mental health disorders</a>. In addition to her medical practice, Dr. Crawford is an author, blogger, podcast host, and public speaker.</p><p dir="ltr"><br/></p></div></div><grammarly-extension-vbars class="dnXmp" data-grammarly-shadow-root="true" style="display: contents; --rem: 16;"></grammarly-extension-vbars><grammarly-extension-vbars class="dnXmp" data-grammarly-shadow-root="true" style="display: contents; --rem: 16;"></grammarly-extension-vbars></div></div></div><grammarly-extension-vbars class="dnXmp" data-grammarly-shadow-root="true" style="display: contents; --rem: 16;"></grammarly-extension-vbars></div>
